   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia Aid</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pacific Climate Finance Access and Effectiveness</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">An Australian investment in climate finance access and effectiveness aligns with the Australian Government&#x2019;s increased climate ambition and responds to requests from Pacific partners. The modality of embedded advisers supports in depth understanding, long term capacity and Pacific agency in the prioritisation of concept and proposal development. The Climate Finance Access Network project enables the development of high-quality project pipelines, concept notes and full proposals for green and climate investment. The Governance for Resilient Development in the Pacific (Gov4res) project ensures that Pacific people, especially women and marginalised groups, are more resilient to the impacts of climate change and disasters.  The project works with Pacific national and local governments and Pacific communities, as well as regional organisations, to strengthen decision-making processes and governance systems towards risk-informed and resilient development.</narrative>
  </description>
